2026-11-07T05:53:34.5692465Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5692579Z       "id": "BLOCK-015",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5692716Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5692835Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5694147Z       "unmetReason": "A tagged default-profile Workers journey and desktop/mobile browser journeys exercise assignment with @, due dates with //, the share prompt, notices, reassignment, completion and the overdue state; email, push, chat, API and MCP delivery belong to NOTIF-005/006, MOBILE-004, CHAT-004, API-001 and API-003; independent release acceptance is separate.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5694349Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5700733Z       "requirement": "#### BLOCK-015 — Assigned tasks with due dates\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** A task item (`BLOCK-007`) can carry one assignee and a due date. Typing `@` inside a task assigns the member mentioned, and typing the documented public door or choosing from the date picker sets the due date, which renders in the reader's locale and shows as overdue once it passes. The assignee gets one inbox item when assigned (`NOTIF-001`), by email or push under their delivery settings (`NOTIF-005`, `NOTIF-006`), and one reminder on the due date (`NOTIF-004`). Reassigning notifies the new assignee once and the previous assignee not at all, and an assignee completing their own task notifies no one. Assigning a member who cannot read the page asks the assigner to share the page with them or cancel, and never notifies that member. Completion still records who and when. Tasks are read and changed through the API and MCP (`API-001`, `API-003`) under the same checks. A task item stays a block, and it still never appears in a database view. Protocol and representation details are in [wiki doors](docs/wiki-doors.md).\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a browser journey at 1440 and 390 types a task, assigns it with `@` and sets a due date with the documented public door.\n2. The assignee gets exactly one inbox item and, after a Workers journey advances time, exactly one due-date reminder.\n3. Reassigning notifies only the new assignee.\n4. Assigning a member without access prompts the assigner to share and sends that member nothing.\n5. The task shows as overdue after its due date."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5700923Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5701020Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5701134Z       "id": "BLOCK-016",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5701268Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5701391Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5702398Z       "unmetReason": "A tagged default-profile 1440/390 browser journey and the public HTTP task journey exercise per-reader task reports, completion and the published sign-in notice; Confluence Task Report import belongs to IMP-010. Independent requirement acceptance remains unproven.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5702518Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5708177Z       "requirement": "#### BLOCK-016 — Task reports\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** A body can hold a task report: a live list of tasks filtered by container, ancestor page, label, assignee (including \"the current reader\"), creator, due-date range and state, grouped by page, assignee or due date, and ordered and limited by the author. It follows `BLOCK-010`'s rules: it re-runs when the page is opened, shows when it last ran, shows each reader only the tasks on pages that reader can read, never renders a task on a draft (`LIFE-002`), and says so when its source container is deleted. A reader with edit access to a task's page can complete the task from the report. A published page shows a task report as a sign-in notice and never runs it for anonymous readers, so a public view reveals no task, page title or count. Confluence Task Report macros import as task reports with the same filters, carried and proven by `IMP-010`.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a browser journey embeds a report filtered to one container and one assignee over tasks on three pages.\n2. One reader sees all three tasks.\n3. A reader without access to one of the pages sees the other two, with no count, title or placeholder for the third.\n4. Completing a task from the report updates its page.\n5. Published, the page shows the report as a sign-in notice, and an anonymous reader's view names none of the tasks or pages and makes no API request."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5708299Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5708396Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5708503Z       "id": "NAV-007",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5708641Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5708813Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5709431Z       "unmetReason": "A tagged default-profile 1440/390 browser journey and the public HTTP task journey exercise My tasks; independent requirement acceptance remains unproven.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5709548Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5714515Z       "requirement": "#### NAV-007 — My tasks\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Every member has a My tasks view, reachable from Home and the sidebar. It lists the tasks assigned to them and, in a second tab, the tasks they created, across every page they can read. It filters by open, completed and overdue, by container and by due-date range, sorts by due date (undated tasks last), page or container, and paginates stably while tasks change. Completing a task in the list completes it on its page under the page's edit check (`BLOCK-007`). A task leaves the list when its page becomes unreadable to the member, is a draft they cannot read (`LIFE-002`) or is in the trash. Guests see only tasks on pages shared with them.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a browser journey assigns one member three tasks on two pages with different due dates.\n2. Their My tasks view, filtered to open and sorted by due date, lists exactly those three in that order.\n3. Completing one from the list marks it done on its page, and revoking the member's access to one page removes its task from the list on the next load."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5720923Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5721324Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5721775Z       "id": "NOTIF-004",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5722330Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5722868Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5724965Z       "unmetReason": "A tagged default-profile Workers journey exercises page, task and date-mention reminders in three time zones, exactly-once dispatch and revoked access; email, push and chat delivery belong to NOTIF-005/006, MOBILE-004 and CHAT-004; independent release acceptance is separate.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5726320Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5729992Z       "requirement": "#### NOTIF-004 — Reminders\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** A date mention (`BLOCK-005`) can carry a reminder at the date or at a chosen offset. A member can set a reminder on any page or task item (`BLOCK-007`), and a task with a due date reminds its assignee on that date (`BLOCK-015`). Reminders arrive in the inbox, and by email or push where the member opted in (`NOTIF-005`), at the member's local time, exactly once, and are rechecked against access at delivery.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey sets reminders in two time zones, advances time, and finds exactly one inbox item each at the right local time.\n2. A reminder on a page whose access was revoked is not delivered."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5732339Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5732751Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5733074Z       "id": "SEARCH-010",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5733517Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5733965Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5734946Z       "unmetReason": "Public HTTP operator, permission, saved-query, trust and duplicate grouping journeys support implementation. Independent requirement acceptance remains unproven.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5735839Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5739164Z       "requirement": "#### SEARCH-010 — Labels and advanced search\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Search and container views filter by label. Queries accept the operators `title:`, `label:`, `in:` (container), `by:` (contributor), `owner:`, `status:`, `verified:`, `before:`, `after:`, `type:` and quoted phrases, combined with `AND`, `OR` and `-`. A member can save a search, and a saved search can feed a content query (`BLOCK-010`). Operators never widen access (`SEARCH-005`).\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey over seeded pages checks each operator and each combination against expected result IDs for two members with different grants.\n2. A browser journey saves a search and embeds it in a page."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5741745Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5742071Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5742441Z       "id": "SEARCH-011",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5742846Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5743323Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5744647Z       "unmetReason": "A tagged default-profile 1440/390 browser journey and the public HTTP search journey exercise verified-first ranking, trust badges, near-duplicate collapse and title-only anonymous views; answer trust belongs to ANSWER-002. Independent requirement acceptance remains unproven.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5746026Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5752711Z       "requirement": "#### SEARCH-011 — Verified-first ranking and trust badges\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Search results, link cards, content queries and answers show each page's verification state (verified with its owner and expiry, lapsed, or unverified) and its last-updated time. Among equally relevant results, ranking puts current verified pages ahead of unverified ones and lapsed or archived pages last, and collapses near-duplicates into one result with a \"similar pages\" control. Anonymous published views of link cards and content queries carry no verification owner, expiry or lapse state; they show titles only. Answers carry this trust under `ANSWER-002`, which proves it. Two pages are near-duplicates when the Jaccard similarity of their current revisions' 5-word shingles, estimated by MinHash, is at least `seed.json → limits.nearDuplicateSimilarity` (0.8 by default); the same definition drives `KEEP-004`. A member can sort by relevance, last updated or most viewed.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey over a seeded corpus of a verified, a lapsed and an unverified page with equal text matches asserts their order and badges.\n2. A seeded pair at a measured similarity of 0.85 collapses into one result and a pair at 0.7 does not; lowering the limit to 0.65 collapses the second pair too.\n3. A browser journey sees the badges and the collapsed near-duplicates, and an anonymous reader of the published pages and of a published content query over them sees their titles with no verification owner, expiry or lapse state."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5758180Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5758577Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5758932Z       "id": "PAGE-016",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5759336Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5759803Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5760987Z       "unmetReason": "Production Workers journeys support durable watches, preferences, lifecycle-aware delivery and personal Following. Independent browser and full requirement acceptance remain unproven; CONT-012 digest delivery remains missing.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5762111Z       "supportingTests": [
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5762516Z         {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5763008Z           "file": "tests/flagship/discovery/following.test.ts",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5763869Z           "testName": "PAGE-016 — authoring watches respect durable unwatch, personal overrides and workspace defaults"
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5764576Z         }
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5764915Z       ],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5768809Z       "requirement": "#### PAGE-016 — Autowatch on create and edit\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Creating a page, or saving an edit to it, watches it for that member, as commenting already does (`PAGE-009`), until they unwatch it. Unwatching stops autowatch for that page, so a later edit by the same member does not watch it again. A member can turn autowatch off for themselves, and `NOTIF-006` sets the workspace default. An implicit watch delivers the same events as an explicit one.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey has one member create a page and a second member edit another page, then a third member comments on both, and the creator and the editor each get exactly one notification.\n2. After the editor unwatches their page and edits it again, a further comment notifies them of nothing.\n3. A member with autowatch off creates a page and is not watching it."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5771855Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5772217Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5772608Z       "id": "CONT-012",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5773009Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5773462Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5774838Z       "unmetReason": "A tagged default-profile Workers journey and desktop/mobile browser journeys exercise container watches, session coalescing, deduplication, posts, restricted and draft suppression and Home's Following section; digest delivery belongs to NOTIF-005; independent release acceptance is separate.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5776251Z       "supportingTests": [
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5776784Z         {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5777255Z           "file": "tests/flagship/discovery/following.test.ts",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5778591Z           "testName": "CONT-012 — a watched container delivers creation, two edit sessions and a comment once each, nothing for restricted or draft pages, one item when the page is also watched, and rechecks moves, lifecycle and access"
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5779652Z         }
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5780002Z       ],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5785877Z       "requirement": "#### CONT-012 — Watch a container\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** A member can watch a whole container. For each page in it the member can read, a watched container delivers page creation, edits, moves in or out, archiving or trashing, and comments and replies, as one inbox item each (`NOTIF-002`) or as one line each in a digest under `NOTIF-005`. Edits are coalesced into one item per page, per author, per editing session (`COLLAB-005`'s window). A page the member cannot read, and every draft (`LIFE-002`), produces nothing. A member who watches both a page and its container gets one item, not two. Blog posts (`CONT-010`) arrive the same way. Home shows a Following section with the same events for the member's watched pages and containers; it is personal, not a workspace-wide feed (`NAV-001`). A container's administrators can see its watchers.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey has a member watch a container.\n2. Another member then creates a page, edits it in two sessions, comments on it, and creates a restricted page the watcher cannot read.\n3. The watcher gets exactly four items (the creation, two edit sessions and the comment) and nothing for the restricted page, and a comment on a page they also watch directly arrives once.\n4. A variant with a daily digest preference finds the same four events as digest lines, and a browser journey sees them in Home's Following section."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5790859Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5791215Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5791554Z       "id": "CONT-010",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5792041Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5792427Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5793612Z       "unmetReason": "Native posts, permission-aware feeds, follower notices and Home are proven by Workers and 1440/390 browser journeys. Genuine incumbent Confluence blog import, Server/DC XML blog posts and NOTIF-005 email delivery remain unproven.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5794756Z       "supportingTests": [
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5795144Z         {
