2026-11-07T05:53:34.5797239Z         },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5797564Z         {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5798050Z           "file": "tests/e2e/imports/blog-posts.test.ts",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5798924Z           "testName": "CONT-010 — a Confluence Cloud blog post imports as a post with its date and author, and undo removes it"
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5799587Z         }
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5799937Z       ],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5802841Z       "requirement": "#### CONT-010 — Space blog and announcements\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** A container has a blog: dated posts with an author, a cover and comments that appear in a feed in the container and on followers' home pages (`NAV-001`). Following a container notifies its followers of new posts (`NOTIF-001`). Posts are pages and keep every page clause. Confluence blogs import as posts (`IMP-003`), not as folders.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a browser journey in which one member publishes a post, a follower gets the notification and sees the post on Home, and importing a Confluence space with blog posts creates posts that keep their dates and authors."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5805265Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.5805602Z     {
