2026-11-07T05:53:34.6313126Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6313418Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6313758Z       "unmetReason": "see the clause",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6314079Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6317097Z       "requirement": "#### SEARCH-012 — Connected results in search\n\n*Tier:* Core · *Register:* R-1\n\n**Requirement.** When connectors are attached (`CONNECT-001`), one search covers Slate content and connected items, which are labeled with their source and opened in their source. Each connected result is shown only if the asking member's mapped identity can read it in the source now (`CONNECT-002`). Connected results never change Slate result ranking for members without that source.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey with a provider fake at the network edge returns a Drive file to a member mapped to its reader and hides it from an unmapped member, with identical Slate results for both."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6319409Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6319618Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6319853Z       "id": "SEARCH-013",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6320145Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6320434Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6320766Z       "unmetReason": "not implemented",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6321087Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6330378Z       "requirement": "#### SEARCH-013 — Search inside attached files\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Slate extracts the text of every attachment of a type `BLOCK-021` previews and indexes it with the page. That covers PDF text layers, Office and OpenDocument text, slide text and speaker notes, sheet cell values, plain text, Markdown and code. Extraction reads the latest version (`BLOCK-022`), up to `seed.json → limits.attachmentTextBytes` per file. When AI is on (`AI-001`), image-only PDFs and images are read by the owner's configured provider and indexed the same way. - **Results.** Global search (`SEARCH-001`) matches attachment text within its 500ms bound. A match is returned as the file, naming its page, with a snippet from the file and the match highlighted. Opening it opens the viewer at the matching page, sheet or slide. Search can be filtered to attachments, and by file type (`SEARCH-010`). - **Access.** `SEARCH-005` applies unchanged: a member without access to the page gets no result, snippet, facet or total from its files. - **Freshness.** A new version is re-indexed through the page's dirty generation (`PORT-004`), and text from an older version stops matching. - **Limits.** A file whose text exceeds the limit shows \"partially indexed\". A file with no extractable text shows \"no searchable text\" while AI is off. - **Answers.** Cited answers (`ANSWER-001`) may cite attachment text. The citation opens the viewer at the cited version and page.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. A Workers journey attaches a PDF and a `.docx` whose bodies each contain a phrase found nowhere else, plus an `.xlsx` and a `.pptx` with their own phrases.\n2. Searching each phrase returns that file and its page with a snippet from the file.\n3. A browser journey opens the viewer at the matching page. - A member without access to the page gets no result, snippet, facet or total for any of the phrases. - Uploading version 2 without the phrase makes the phrase stop matching once indexing settles. - A file larger than the text limit shows \"partially indexed\". - With AI on and a provider fake at the network edge, a scanned PDF's phrase becomes searchable. - An import of the `IMP-007` fixture has its attachment text searchable before the import is Completed (`PORT-004`)."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6337616Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6337836Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6338082Z       "id": "SEARCH-014",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6338381Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
