2026-11-07T05:53:34.6362342Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6362637Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6362945Z       "unmetReason": "see the clause",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6363264Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6366882Z       "requirement": "#### CARD-001 — Knowledge cards and collections\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** A card is a short page kind with a soft length limit (`seed.json → limits`, 500 words by default: past it the editor warns and suggests a page, and nothing is truncated), a question-style title, an owner, verification required by default, and placement in a collection (a container with card-friendly views). Cards render compactly in search, answers, chat (`CHAT-002`) and the browser extension (`CARD-002`). Guru cards import as cards (`IMP-008`).\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a browser journey creates a card and finds it as a compact result with its verification badge, and a 600-word card shows the length warning and saves intact.\n2. A Guru import creates cards in collections that keep their owners and their verification intervals as imported metadata."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6369665Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6369874Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6370105Z       "id": "CARD-002",
