2026-11-07T05:53:34.6436992Z       "unmetReason": "see the clause",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6437105Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6440970Z       "requirement": "#### AUTO-006 — Outbound automation actions\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Rule actions (`AUTO-001`) can also: - post to a Slack, Microsoft Teams or Nook channel; - call a signed webhook (`API-002`); - send an email from a member's own connected Gmail or Outlook mailbox under that member's OAuth grant, never from Slate's sender (`MAIL-001`); - create a Vector or Jira issue, with a backlink to the page (`EMBED-005`). Each action acts as the rule's actor (`AUTO-002`), sends only titles, links and fields the actor can read, uses an operation key so retries never duplicate, and records its receipt in the run log (`AUTO-003`). Protocol and representation details are in [wiki doors](docs/wiki-doors.md).\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey with provider fakes at the network edge fires one rule four times and finds one message, one webhook, one email and one issue per firing.\n2. A retried firing produces no duplicate, and every receipt appears in the run log."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441089Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441185Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441295Z       "id": "AUTO-007",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441429Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441548Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441691Z       "unmetReason": "not implemented",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6441807Z       "supportingTests": [],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6444350Z       "requirement": "#### AUTO-007 — Triggers from connected tools\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Rules can trigger on events from connected tools: a GitHub or GitLab pull request merged or released, a Vector or Jira issue changing state, a Drive file changing, or an inbound signed webhook. They can then flag a page, request review, create a record or start a `KEEP-001` check. Event payloads are untrusted content (`AI-007`).\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey posts a signed GitHub-shaped webhook and sees the matching rule run once and request review on the linked page.\n2. An unsigned or replayed delivery is rejected and logged."
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6444466Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6444562Z     {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6444672Z       "id": "AUTO-008",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6444804Z       "document": "CONTRACT.md",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6444921Z       "status": "unproven",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6448035Z       "unmetReason": "Native automation-rule acceptance 1 is exercised by automationRestartJourney through the existing desktop database run-log caller: a genuinely killed emitted Worker, same persistent store, genuine lease boundary, canonical record, comment and inbox effects, receipt and activity reconciliation and replay. The existing automation-repairs Workers registration retains supporting exception recovery and authority checks. Other background-job families, owner Home failure and stuck projection, explicit stop and cancellation, complete accountable follow-through and message, record and issue deduplication remain unproven. Connector, agent, provider, ADMIN-007 and shared company-policy prerequisites remain authoritative. CONTRACT.md owns the partial judgment; exact candidate Verify and guarded landing remain required.",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6448282Z       "supportingTests": [
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6448388Z         {
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6448638Z           "file": "tests/flagship/structured/automation-repairs.test.ts",
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6449066Z           "testName": "automation admission, resumed effects and schedules preserve current scope and exactly-once recovery"
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6449171Z         }
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6449284Z       ],
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6452416Z       "requirement": "#### AUTO-008 — Accountable follow-through\n\n*Tier:* Core\n\n**Requirement.** Every background action is a durable job with an accountable owner, a due condition, visible progress, a visible failure and an explicit stop or resolution state. This covers rules, schedules, reminders, review escalations, connector syncs, verification rules and agent work. A failed or stuck job appears on the owner's Home without a search. Re-running a job never duplicates a message, record or issue, and stopping a job cancels its unsent work.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. a Workers journey kills a job mid-run and finds it resumed once with no duplicate effect.\n2. A forced failure appears on the owner's Home, and stopping a queued job cancels its pending sends.\n\n\n### Moving in and out"
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6452541Z     },
2026-11-07T05:53:34.6452643Z     {
