nsitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.answers.ask` | Answers — ask | AI-015, ANSWER-001, ANSWER-002, ANSWER-003, ANSWER-004, KEEP-005 | standard or external (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.summaries.run` | Summaries — run | AI-016, ANSWER-005 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.writing.transform` | Writing — transform | AI-017 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.decisions.manage` | Decisions — manage | DEC-001, DEC-002, DEC-003, DEC-004, DEC-005, DEC-006 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.suggestions.manage` | Suggestions — manage | SUG-001, SUG-002 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.connectors.configure` | Connectors — configure | SOURCE-001, SOURCE-006, CONNECT-001 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.claims.manage` | Claims — manage | SOURCE-003 | standard (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.sources.sync` | Sources — sync | SOURCE-004, SOURCE-005, CONNECT-002, CONNECT-003 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.skills.manage` | Skills — manage | SKILL-001 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.skills.evaluate_and_activate` | Skills — evaluate and activate | SKILL-002 | standard or external (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.skills.transition` | Skills — transition | SKILL-003 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.effects.manage` | Effects — manage | EFFECT-001 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | prepare_effect, dispatch_effect, reconcile_effect (partial) |\n| `slate.activation.manage` | Activation — manage | EFFECT-002 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.impact.rehearse_and_apply` | Impact — rehearse and apply | EFFECT-003 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.inquiries.manage` | Inquiries — manage | INQ-001, INQ-002, INQ-003, INQ-004, INQ-005 | standard (+ sensitive) | inquiry_status (partial) |\n| `slate.trials.plan` | Trials — plan | TRIAL-001 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.trials.execute` | Trials — execute | TRIAL-002 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.trials.conclude` | Trials — conclude | TRIAL-003 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.learning.update` | Learning — update | TRIAL-004 | standard or external (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.pages.lock` | Pages — lock | PAGE-015 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.tasks.update` | Tasks — update | BLOCK-015 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.tasks.report` | Tasks — report | BLOCK-016 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.attachments.replace` | Attachments — replace | BLOCK-022 | standard or external (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.blog.manage` | Blog — manage | CONT-010 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.hub.configure` | Hub — configure | CONT-011 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.people.manage` | People — manage | WORK-016 | standard or external (+ access) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.tasks.list` | Tasks — list | NAV-007 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.reviews.manage` | Reviews — manage | STAT-006 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.verification_rules.configure` | Verification rules — configure | STAT-007 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.cards.manage` | Cards — manage | CARD-001 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.reading.manage` | Reading — manage | CARD-003 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.forms.manage` | Forms — manage | DB-013 | standard or external (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.dashboards.configure` | Dashboards — configure | DB-014 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.record_templates.configure` | Record templates — configure | DB-015 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.fields.autofill` | Fields — autofill | DB-016 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.reminders.set` | Reminders — set | NOTIF-004 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.notification_preferences.configure` | Notification preferences — configure | NOTIF-005, NOTIF-006, CHAT-004 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.rules.execute` | Rules — execute | AUTO-006 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.jobs.manage` | Jobs — manage | AUTO-008 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.backups.configure` | Backups — configure | PORT-009 | standard or external (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.embeds.read` | Embeds — read | EMBED-001, EMBED-002, EMBED-003, EMBED-004, EMBED-007, EMBED-008 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.issues.link_back` | Issues — link back | EMBED-005 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.jira.cutover_links` | Jira — cutover links | EMBED-006 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.chat.ask_or_unfurl` | Chat — ask or unfurl | CHAT-002 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.chat.capture` | Chat — capture | CHAT-003 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.webhooks.manage` | Webhooks — manage | API-002 | standard or external (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.clients.manage` | Clients — manage | API-004 | standard (+ access) (+ security) | not exposed |\n| `slate.directory.configure` | Directory — configure | ADMIN-002 | standard or external (+ access) (+ security) | not exposed |\n| `slate.analytics.report` | Analytics — report | ADMIN-004 | standard (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.audit.export_and_stream` | Audit — export and stream | ADMIN-005 | standard or external (+ access) (+ security) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.governance.configure` | Governance — configure | ADMIN-006 | standard or external (+ access) (+ security) | not exposed |\n| `slate.features.configure` | Features — configure | ADMIN-007 | standard or external (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) | not exposed |\n| `slate.knowledge.check` | Knowledge — check | KEEP-001 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.knowledge.repair` | Knowledge — repair | KEEP-002 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.knowledge.request_evidence` | Knowledge — request evidence | KEEP-003 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.knowledge.reconcile` | Knowledge — reconcile | KEEP-004 | standard or external (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.runbooks.check` | Runbooks — check | KEEP-006 | standard or external (+ money) (+ commitment) (+ accounts) (+ gated) (+ access) (+ security) (+ destructive) (+ sensitive) (+ live) | not exposed |\n| `slate.onboarding.prepare` | Onboarding — prepare | KEEP-007 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.knowledge.sweep` | Knowledge — sweep | KEEP-008 | standard or external (+ commitment) (+ access) (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n| `slate.knowledge_health.read` | Knowledge health — read | KEEP-009 | standard (+ sensitive) | not exposed |\n\n**Resources.** `slate://containers/{id}`, `slate://pages/{id}`, `slate://pages/{id}/revisions/{revision}`, `slate://blocks/{id}`, `slate://databases/{id}`, `slate://records/{id}`, `slate://threads/{id}`, `slate://sources/{id}/passages/{passage}`, `slate://decisions/{id}`, `slate://inquiries/{id}`, `slate://runs/{id}`.\n\n**Events.** Page and block changes, task assignments and completions, verification changes, suggestions, decisions, source changes, inquiries, run outcomes and the inherited policy, approval and review events.\n\n**Prompts.** Curate a week of knowledge (KEEP-001 to KEEP-010, SURFACE-006), answer with current citations (ANSWER-001 to ANSWER-006), investigate an open question (INQ-001 to INQ-005), and evaluate a predeclared trial (TRIAL-001 to TRIAL-004).\n\n**Not tools, and why.**\n\n| Core clauses | Reason |\n| --- | --- |\n| HOME-001 | An installation fact and a public reader screen; no private operation is performed. |\n| HOME-002 | An installation fact and a public reader screen; no private operation is performed. |\n| HOME-003 | An installation fact and a public reader screen; no private operation is performed. |\n| DOCS-001 | A public documentation screen; record operations are the tools documented there. |\n| WORK-012 | A person’s theme preference screen. |\n| WORK-014 | A person’s keyboard shortcut screen. |\n| PAGE-010 | A person’s outline navigation screen. |\n| PAGE-011 | A person’s presentation screen. |\n| BLOCK-003 | A person’s insert-menu screen; block creation and editing are tools. |\n| BLOCK-004 | A person’s typing interaction; the resulting block edits are tools. |\n| NAV-004 | A person’s responsive navigation screen. |\n| NAV-006 | A person’s touch editing screen; its record actions are tools. |\n| IMP-001 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-015 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-002 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-003 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-016 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-004 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-005 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| FLAG-001 | An installation and release-qualification fact; its wiki operations are tools in their own rows. |\n| FLAG-002 | An installation and release-qualification fact; its wiki operations are tools in their own rows. |\n| FLAG-003 | An installation and release-qualification fact; its wiki operations are tools in their own rows. |\n| FLAG-004 | An installation and release-qualification fact; its wiki operations are tools in their own rows. |\n| COLLAB-002 | Device cursor and viewport presence; page edits are tools. |\n| COLLAB-004 | An installation capacity fact measured through browser and collaboration doors. |\n| CARD-002 | A browser-device extension; its search and record actions are tools. |\n| IMP-006 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-007 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-008 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-009 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-010 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-011 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-012 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-013 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| IMP-014 | The import door performs archive and provider migration jobs; it is not a second MCP import implementation. |\n| MOBILE-001 | Device-only native UI, biometric, offline-storage or operating-system delivery work; its record actions use the ordinary tools. |\n| MOBILE-002 | Device-only native UI, biometric, offline-storage or operating-system delivery work; its record actions use the ordinary tools. |\n| MOBILE-003 | Device-only native UI, biometric, offline-storage or operating-system delivery work; its record actions use the ordinary tools. |\n| MOBILE-004 | Device-only native UI, biometric, offline-storage or operating-system delivery work; its record actions use the ordinary tools. |\n| SAVE-001 | A person’s editor save-state display; the page and block write tools return the committed receipt. |\n| SAVE-002 | A person’s failed-save and retry display; page and block tools return the same refusal and retained revision. |\n| SAVE-004 | Device-only offline draft recovery; committed writes use the normal page and block tools. |\n| WORK-013 | A person’s first-run and owner-claim screen; the resulting workspace is an installation fact. |\n| BLOCK-021 | A person’s in-page and full-screen preview viewers; file resources supply permitted originals and renditions. |\n| AGENT-002 | An owner’s source-customization and installation fact; record and interface data remain available through their normal reads and exports. |\n| API-001 | The REST transport and its OpenAPI description are installation facts; its page, block, record, comment, search, member, group and file jobs are tools below. |\n| API-005 | Connector-managed Zapier, Make and Crank apps; their record actions use the same individual tools and event feed. |\n| API-003 | The MCP transport is an installation fact; its search, page, database, answer, comment and task jobs are the individual tools below. |\n| AI-011 | A wiki authority invariant on every action; grant and client administration have their own actions, and people set company policy. |\n| AI-012 | A person’s company-policy and provider-spend setup screen, under the fixed rule that people set policy; usage is a read tool. |\n| MAIL-001 | An installation mail-transport fact; invitation and notification actions trigger its permitted messages. |\n\n**Limits.** The installation's documented request, body, byte and computation capacity applies. Business thresholds and provider-spend caps are company policy, including an explicit no-cap answer.\n\n**Handoffs.** Listen for typed issue, source-document and support knowledge events from Vector/Jira, Chest/Drive/SharePoint and HappyToHelp; emit cited knowledge, review, task, inquiry and outcome events. Conversation sending stays in the conversation product and CRM outreach in Orbit. Policy decides each agent call's declared classes."
